# ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# ICP website — environment variables (sample)
#
# Copy this file to `.env` (or `.env.local`) and fill in real values.
# Variables prefixed with VITE_ are exposed to the client bundle.
#
# IMPORTANT: real values belong in `.env`, never in this file.
# `.env` is gitignored; `.env.example` is committed to the repo, so
# anything placed here (including access keys) becomes public history.
# ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Contact form endpoint.
# Examples:
#   Formspree   → https://formspree.io/f/<your-form-id>
#   Web3Forms   → https://api.web3forms.com/submit
#                 (also requires VITE_CONTACT_ACCESS_KEY below)
#
# If unset, the contact form falls back to a mailto: handoff using
# icpeip012@gmail.com so it always remains usable in production.
VITE_CONTACT_ENDPOINT=

# Web3Forms access key (from https://web3forms.com → your form's
# dashboard). Required only when VITE_CONTACT_ENDPOINT points at
# Web3Forms — its API rejects submissions without it. Leave unset for
# Formspree, which doesn't need one.
VITE_CONTACT_ACCESS_KEY=

# Google Analytics 4 Measurement ID (e.g. G-XXXXXXXXXX).
# Get this at https://analytics.google.com → Admin → Data Streams →
# your web stream. When unset, the gtag bootstrap in index.html
# short-circuits and analytics never loads — useful for local dev
# and preview branches.
VITE_GA_MEASUREMENT_ID=
